# Four Roles (Agent Requested) — lightweight port of OmO's agent roster

OmO's specialized agents (Sisyphus/Hephaestus/Prometheus/...) compressed to **4 roles** for MVP work. Each defines "when / which paperthin skills / which model tier". Promoting them to Cursor **Custom Modes** is convenient (register each role as a mode).

## 🧭 Plan — plan & review
- **When**: before starting a task/feature; setting direction.
- **paperthin**: `/readchk` (confirm the request was read right — don't perfectly build the wrong thing), `/hate` (the one objection that could kill the plan), `/feynman` (can you explain the decision), `/modelchk` (size this task's tier).
- **Model**: usually standard. Frontier only for a short review of high-risk work (auth/payment/design forks).

## 🔎 Explore — research & discovery
- **When**: gathering information, code, or context.
- **Tools**: research MCP (order & output per `research`), Cursor **explore subagent** (parallel codebase search = OmO Explore).
- **paperthin**: `/factchk` (verify claims both ways), `/macrothink` (strip bait, fan out fresh reads), `/catchup` (rebuild lost context on re-entry).
- **Model**: fast~standard. (No frontier for exploration.)
- **Boundary**: surfaces evidence/options only; **does not decide direction/value** (that's Plan/human). `research` = the tool method, Explore = the role that uses it.

## 🔨 Build — implementation
- **When**: writing actual code.
- **paperthin**: `/aim` (fix intent from handed-over data), `/autobahn` (carve out risky scope up front, run the safe rest at full strength), `/sip` (auto quality-check right after a change).
- **Model**: standard (Grok/Composer). Don't run long build loops on frontier.

## ✅ Review — review & cleanup
- **When**: after an artifact exists, before commit/submit.
- **paperthin**: `/shower` (cold read with fresh eyes), `/re0` (rewrite a drifted artifact as a clean v0, don't patch), `/debloat` (compress bloat), `/ssotize` (consolidate scattered facts), `/sip`; for claims/evals also `/factchk`, `/mandela`.
- **Model**: fast~standard. (Review is usually fine on a cheap tier.)

## Flow
Run Plan → Explore → Build → Review. Judgment stays with the human (`harness-core`). Long autonomous work follows `autonomous` + `context-loop`.
